(Plan 230 stage A4 — version 1.0 of `parts`, linked with parts_0_1.vox into one
.so. Exports `common` (so a consumer importing both versions finds it twice —
the ambiguity dual) AND `only one` (which 0.1 does NOT export, so a consumer
importing both versions and calling `only one` finds exactly one provider and
resolves without a warning). `common` returns n add 100 here so the two
versions' bodies are distinct, the same pattern as flags.)

Library "parts" version "1.0".

To "common" with a number called "n".
  Return a number, n add 100.

To "only one" with a number called "n".
  Return a number, n add 42.